atus":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0020. The audit report and four proposals meet the goal, and nothing below needs fixing before approval.\n\n- **Goal:** `AUD-1.md` follows the auditor format: a scoreboard of indicators, verdicts on earlier proposals (\"none yet\", which is correct), observations O1 to O8, proposals, and \"what not to change\". Each of TEP-0001 to TEP-0004 states a hypothesis the next audit can test, how to check it, and its risks. With 18 distinct packets, every rule touched fewer than 20, so calling all results observations rather than findings is correct.\n- **Numbers:** I re-added the costs in `packets.jsonl` and got $19.44 over 22 records, which matches the report.\n- **Contract:** the diff only adds files under `.theseus/audits` and `.theseus/proposals`, plus the packet log and one friction line, which the rules require. That is 7 files and 188 lines, within the budget of 8 files and 1,500 lines.\n- **TEP-0004 checks:**\n  - The Executor log is filled in.\n  - No follow-ups were requested; the executor says every gap is in the method, not the project.\n  - The friction line is present and well-formed.\n\n**Weaknesses to note, not blocking:**\n1. **O4 overstates a rule conflict.** It says same-family review conflicts with the cross-family rule \"unless\" pilot mode is on, but the executor never checked. `.theseus/adapter/adapter.yaml:85` sets `review.allow_same_family: true`, so the period's same-family reviews were allowed. The real point is weaker: the review results can't tell us whether cross-family review would do better. Same-family auditing is a separate matter, and it still goes against the measurement spec's \"Who audits\" section.\n2. **Shallow sources.** The executor didn't read `scoreboard/runs/` or the packet logs in depth, though the packet lists the run folders as context. O1 (outside dependencies) and O8 (lost knowledge) rest on rejection reasons and friction lines only. The log says so openly, and the conclusions still hold.\n3. **This packet's own check is weak.** Its only acceptance command is `test -s`, which just checks the file isn't empty. The executor flagged this (it is the weakness TEP-0003 targets), so this review was the real check on the content.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Audit complete, numbers check out, within scope and budget; O4 should note that pilot mode is on (`allow_same_family: true`).","ttft_ms":2170,"type":"result","duration_ms":18312,"uuid":"49e188b1-2ea3-4e38-ab65-f50591cf0a01","ttft_stream_ms":963,"time_to_request_ms":350,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":206,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":18,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":20,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":12,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":10,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":33,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":2,"request_build":11},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":62,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":182,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":214,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":228,"process_anon_mib_result":138,"process_peak_rss_mib":256,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1112,"process_wall_ms_turn":18312,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":510,"process_wall_ms_streaming":14981,"main_stream_count":5,"main_stream_event_count":295,"main_stream_chunk_count":100,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":7,"cpu_ms":20,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":7,"ambient_wait_ms":7,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":963,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":4210632,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793639667210.4827,"queued_turn_count":0,"resul